[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome. I\'m so grateful that you\'ve joined us here today and it\'s going to be a lot of fun and mostly live demos because the goal of the show today is to'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you how specs work and what they do so you\'re ready to go hands-on right after the show. So, I will say it\'s an interesting time'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to be launching a new computer because things in tech are pretty weird right now. We\'re being told that AI will take our'

[04:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'jobs, that virtual worlds will replace the real one. Well, no thank you. We do not accept that future.'

[04:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Making people irrelevant is not progress. And computers should make us more important, not less. So our bet is on you,'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on your imagination, on your creativity, on what you can build, and on what we can do together. Because technology should add to your'

[05:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'life, not cut you out of it. So more than a decade ago, we set out to rebuild the computer from the ground up around what\'s most important,'

[05:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people. And that gave birth to specs and our vision for making computing more human. And we started with how people actually interact with the world. And it\'s a miracle of evolutionary biology, but'

[05:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it\'s really quite simple. We look at what\'s around us, we think about it, and then we act on it. And we do that over and over and over again.'

[06:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, we built specs to support that same interaction. And that\'s why specs are glasses. So, they can see what you see. They can understand the worlds without'

[06:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'recording it, just like you. And specs bring digital experiences into the world with seeth through lenses, so you can keep your head up and your hands'

[06:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'free. And you interact naturally using familiar movements with your hands and your voice. And we call this instinctual computing because you don\'t have to'

[06:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'learn anything new. You just use your natural instincts to navigate specs experiences. So you can reach out and grab an object or just ask for what you want. And it really is that simple.'

[06:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Because getting things done shouldn\'t mean choosing what app to use, logging in, then copy pasting information from one app to another.'

[07:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, we built the first ever AI native operating system with intelligence designed around your projects, your preferences, and your interests. And it helps connect the dots across lenses so'

[07:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can get things done while focusing on what matters to you. And humanity is inherently social. So we built shared experiences into the'

[07:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'foundation of our operating system so that people can naturally and easily use computing together. We can learn from each other, build on each other\'s ideas, and create things'

[07:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that we never would have made alone. Being together is part of what makes us human. So it needs to be a part of computing, too.'

[07:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Specs help you do the things you care about. in the real world. Learning to shoot a basketball with the ball in your hands. Learning to draw with the outline projected in front of you. And specs can'

[08:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'help, but you\'re the one taking the shot. You\'re the one holding the pen. You\'re building the skill. You\'re making something. And for us, winning means people'

[08:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spending more time together doing the things they love, empowered to make a positive impact in the world. Because the future isn\'t about what computers can do. It\'s about what you'

[08:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can do. And we\'re just getting started. So, back in June, we introduced Specs AR glasses and showed the world what we\'ve been working on for the past 12 years.'

[08:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We got some great feedback, including some pretty funny memes. There\'s even some new ear merch, which'

[09:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'part of me wanted to wear that today, but [laughter] then people began to really understand that we\'re building something different. Not a VR headset that shuts you out of'

[09:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the world. A new kind of computer built into a pair of see-through glasses. But above all, people just wanted to try'

[09:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'specs. So, guess what? Today is the day. [cheering] [applause]'

[09:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [applause] &gt;&gt; But before we really get going, wanted to let you in on a little secret'

[09:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because specs aren\'t just AR glasses. Our team told me that would be way too easy. Specs are part of an intelligence system'

[10:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that lives across your Mac and your iPhone. And we call this specs intelligence. Specs intelligence provides proactive'

[10:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'recommendations based on your real world context. And it connects to the apps and tools that you already use. It learns your goals and priorities, and it helps you focus on what matters most.'

[10:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, let me show you what I mean. &gt;&gt; Most software waits for you. It waits for you to open an app, remember a task, or figure out the right questions to'

[10:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ask. &gt;&gt; But life doesn\'t work that way. You\'re moving between meetings, traveling, or just trying to keep track of work and family. [music] You don\'t need another inbox or chatbot. &gt;&gt; This is Specs Intelligence. It connects across three services, Mac,'

[11:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'iPhone, and Specs. On Mac, Specs brings together your everyday apps like email, calendar, and notes to clear out the daily digital noise. &gt;&gt; On iPhone, that same intelligence moves'

[11:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with you throughout [music] the day. &gt;&gt; And on the glasses, it becomes part of your surroundings. If you\'re traveling for a busy weekend, [music] Specs coordinates your flight'

[11:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'details, hotel reservations, and reminders. &gt;&gt; Hey, Specs, what\'s the latest on my trip? &gt;&gt; Your flight got switched to gate 14. Take your time heading in. &gt;&gt; Under the hood, Specs builds a private'

[11:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'context layer around your life, your portrait, your key corners, and your long-term goals. &gt;&gt; Your portrait is Spec\'s understanding [music] of you, your people, your work, your patterns, and the things you care about. Corners help Specs organize'

[11:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different parts of your life like work, family, travel, health, and relationships [music] so the right things surface at the right moments. &gt;&gt; And goals help Specs understand [music] the bigger things you\'re working toward, not just the tasks in front of you.'

[12:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Together, that\'s what lets Specs help you move with more intention, not just keep up. &gt;&gt; And when it handles the busy work, like drafting a message or cancelling a subscription you\'ve been meaning to cancel, it always asks before taking'

[12:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'action. [music] You stay completely in control. &gt;&gt; That trust is built on privacy. You decide which apps and devices to connect. So you decide what Spec [music] sees and what it does. &gt;&gt; You don\'t need the glasses to get'

[12:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'started. You can try Specs intelligence on Mac and iPhone to experience a [music] clearer, more intentional way to move through your day. &gt;&gt; So you can spend less time managing information and more time living. [applause]'

